    "body": "## Motivation\n\nDiffusion latency guards deliberately reject over-budget CUDA runs but only warn on HIP. Tests must cover both policies without depending on the host GPU.\n\nUpstream #42391 already merged the fixture platform isolation originally proposed here. This PR is now limited to four additional regression cases: E2E/load latency crossed with CUDA/HIP policy. It checks that an in-budget request emits no warning, an over-budget CUDA request raises, and an over-budget HIP request emits exactly one AMD performance warning. Production validators and thresholds are unchanged.\n\n## Validation\n\nSynced with upstream `bab04cd7913ff50d1bf1a677a2d10e5015dc4c3b`. The remaining diff is 21 lines in `test_load_inclusive_e2e.py`.\n\nRTX 5090 D v2, Python 3.12, PyTorch 2.13.0+cu130:\n\n- Native CUDA platform policy: **95 passed**.\n- Simulated HIP platform policy on the same host: **95 passed**. This tests policy dispatch, not AMD kernels.\n- Changed-file pre-commit and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Remote source content was checked against the complete Git index plus working-tree changes before testing.\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest -q \\\n  python/sglang/multimodal_gen/test/unit/test_load_inclusive_e2e.py \\\n  python/sglang/multimodal_gen/test/unit/test_runner_perf_baselines.py \\\n  python/sglang/multimodal_gen/test/unit/test_sequential_server_requests.py\n```\n\nNo inference speedup or native AMD execution is claimed. Codex assisted with implementation and testing.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37233246273](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37233246273)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37233246161](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37233246161)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37233246322](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37233246322)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
